sequenceDiagram
  participant Probe as CUJ probes / regional evidence
  participant IC as Incident Commander
  participant Auth as DR Recovery Authority
  participant Risk as Business / Risk Authority
  participant SSM as SSM Automation
  participant ARC as Route 53 ARC
  participant DB as Aurora Global DB
  participant MSK as MSK Replicator
  participant SG as Singapore primary
  participant DR as Malaysia recovery Region
  participant Ext as External providers
  Probe->>IC: Customer impact + independent regional evidence
  IC->>IC: Declare incident, single alarm alone is insufficient
  IC->>Auth: Request recovery authorization
  Auth->>SSM: Start approved failover runbook
  SSM->>DB: Capture lag / last durable transaction
  SSM->>MSK: Capture replication lag / offsets / topic state
  alt RPO is within target
    SSM->>SSM: Record measured RPO
  else RPO exceeds target or cannot be confirmed
    SSM->>Risk: Request documented RPO exception decision
    alt Exception approved
      Risk-->>SSM: Record approved exception
    else Exception denied
      Risk-->>SSM: Deny exception
      SSM-->>Auth: Abort failover, do not promote
      Note over SSM,ARC: Promotion and traffic switch are skipped
    end
  end
  opt Continue only if RPO target met or exception approved
  SSM->>SG: Fence primary write path
  SG-->>SSM: Confirm old writer cannot accept writes
  alt Write fencing uncertain
    SSM-->>Auth: Stop runbook and escalate
  else Fencing confirmed
    SSM->>DB: Promote Malaysia secondary
    SSM->>MSK: Cut producer/consumer ownership to Malaysia
    SSM->>DR: Activate/scale services and verify IAM, KMS, network, telemetry
    DR->>Ext: Validate provider connectivity / allowlists / status checks
    DR->>DR: Run sign-in, balance, payment preflight and ledger checks
    Auth->>SSM: Approve traffic switch after readiness gate
    SSM->>ARC: Set routing controls to Malaysia (on/off)
    ARC-->>DR: Route customer traffic to Malaysia
    DR->>IC: Report CUJ health, lag, pending age, and duplicate signals
    IC->>IC: Gate A: service restored, Gate B: reconciliation complete
  end
  end

  rect rgb(245, 245, 245)
    Note over Auth,SSM: Failback is a separate approved runbook. Malaysia remains the only writer until synchronization and reconciliation pass.
    Auth->>SSM: Start approved failback after Singapore readiness
    SSM->>DB: Synchronize and verify Aurora state back to Singapore
    SSM->>MSK: Verify topics, offsets, and ownership for Singapore
    SSM->>DR: Reconcile pending payments and delayed events
    SSM->>SG: Validate capacity and critical journeys
    Auth->>SSM: Approve failback routing change
    SSM->>ARC: Set routing controls to Singapore (on/off)
    ARC-->>SG: Route customer traffic to Singapore
  end
